{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pulls/3","id":4790148213,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU_uMns8AAAABHYPcdQ","html_url":"https://github.com/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pull/3","diff_url":"https://github.com/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pull/3.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pull/3.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/issues/3","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pulls/3/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pulls/3/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/issues/3/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/statuses/d4422425750a1d3c4e432cc103ac42ead40b7cc6","number":3,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"v0.5.5: connected compressor capacity control and measured training","user":{"login":"cdehek","id":67599094,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NTk5MDk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67599094?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek","html_url":"https://github.com/cdehek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Live plant gains opt-in single-compressor manual/automatic suction capacity control. Delivered speed drives the conservative refrigerant model; requested speed, sensed/actual suction, targets, limiting reasons and timers remain separate from playback. Legacy manual runs, banks, saved profile schemas and Fahrenheit/psig defaults are preserved.\n\nOrdinary run demand now honors minimum-run timing, while master disable and independent model stops inhibit immediately. Accepted start/rest/demand-stop deadlines include fractional times with linked history evidence. The workspace exposes controls, synchronized curves, SI exports, reset/pending-mode guidance and stop-first range-edit instructions.\n\nThree measured Default lessons cover managed startup, minimum-run demand hold and automatic suction-target response alongside the five preserved legacy lessons. Settings/basis/permission guards prevent unsupported grading; completion pauses at accepted boundaries and freezes the exported controller/history evidence. Timing lessons label shortened illustrative assumptions.\n\nValidation:\n- Local: all 13 numerical and 16 Chromium suites passed.\n- Numerical coverage includes conservation, simultaneous feed/suction PI, ten-minute load/mode operation, high/low saturation recovery, fractional deadlines/refinement, trips/clear evidence, atomic edits, batching, all eight lessons, observer purity and frozen reports.\n- Browser coverage includes actual UI/model/export agreement, managed lessons at 1×/10×/60×, units, guidance, recovery, tablet/phone touch layouts and offline/older-browser operation.\n- Hosted CI passed on `e86da1975dd177248a78d40c114bf76123c173ea`: 13 numerical, 16 Chromium and 7 WebKit suites, plus deterministic source/bundle consistency. [Verify simulator run 37850014665](https://github.com/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/actions/runs/37850014665).\n- Review regressions verify immediately returned telemetry for manual→automatic and automatic→manual transitions without added simulation time or physical changes; priority operating reasons and current limits remain correct. Applied-mode guidance reads the actual settings. Endpoint protection uses the accepted interval's delivered speed, covering demand shutdowns, missed/false discharge trips, idle intervals and starts, with legacy physics/work comparisons.\n- Fresh Codex review of `e86da1975dd177248a78d40c114bf76123c173ea` completed and reported no major issues ([review result](https://github.com/cdehek/Ammonia-sim/pull/3#issuecomment-6069849244)); all previous review threads are resolved.\n- Generalized test report and demonstration checklist: [RELEASE_CHECKS.md](RELEASE_CHECKS.md).\n\nScope: controller/plant coefficients remain illustrative; manufacturer/measured equipment calibration stays v0.6.0. Managed capacity requires one circulating compressor; external demand is explicit, without connected thermostat/bank sequencing or rotor/oil/defrost modeling. WebKit/iPad emulation does not claim physical-device validation.\n\nRelease candidate is 0.5.5. Pages remains at the approved v0.5.0 baseline until approval, merge and deployment.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T16:57:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:42:20Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f440560fccfa45421ec2bf679bac32df10df63ae","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"cdehek:v0.5.5-stage-1","ref":"v0.5.5-stage-1","repo":{"id":1408994462,"node_id":"R_kgDOU_uMng","name":"Ammonia-sim","full_name":"cdehek/Ammonia-sim","owner":{"login":"cdehek","id":67599094,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NTk5MDk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67599094?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek","html_url":"https://github.com/cdehek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdehek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subsc